course: dictionary
lesson: 9933
title: Tapestry: a picture cloth and a rich mix
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tapestry is a heavy piece of cloth with a picture or pattern made by weaving or sewing coloured threads. It is usually hung on a wall, and castles had them to keep rooms warm and colourful. Look for clues like hung on a wall, and the word will make sense.
explain: The word has a second meaning, used in writing. «A rich tapestry of cultures» does not mean a cloth. It means a rich mixture of many different things, woven together like threads of different colours. Ask: does the sentence describe something on a wall, or a mix of many things? The clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Some tapestries are not woven at all. The famous «Bayeux Tapestry» is really an embroidery, stitched with a needle. It keeps the word tapestry in its name, because it is still a picture cloth made by sewing. It tells its story in pictures, like a giant embroidered comic strip.
fact: Tapestry (noun) has two meanings: a picture cloth hung on a wall, and a rich mix of many different things.
fact: «The Bayeux Tapestry» tells the story of the Battle of Hastings in 1066, in pictures.
fact: The Bayeux Tapestry is really an embroidery, made by sewing coloured threads.
fact: «Louise Bourgeois» made giant spider sculptures called «Maman», and she said the spider stood for her mother, who repaired tapestries.
fact: «A rich tapestry of» means a variety of many things, such as cultures, ideas or sounds.
exercise: «The Bayeux Tapestry tells the story of 1066 in pictures.» What is a tapestry here? | A sweet made from honey | *A heavy cloth with a picture made by sewing or weaving coloured threads | A tall, thin tower of stone | A small wooden box
exercise: «The class was a rich tapestry of cultures, with children from many countries.» What does tapestry mean here? | A small wooden box | *A rich mixture of many different things | A stitched map of the world | A heavy cloth hung on a wall
exercise: Castles had tapestries to keep rooms warm and colourful. Why were they hung in castles? | To carry water to the towers | To show the time of day | To keep the rain out of the sea | *To keep rooms warm and colourful
test: «The Bayeux Tapestry tells the story in pictures.» Is the Bayeux Tapestry really woven? | *No, it is an embroidery, made by sewing | It is a stone carving | It is a painting on wood | Yes, it is woven on a loom
test: Ella says «a rich tapestry of cultures» means a heavy cloth. What is the best reply? | It means a tiny tent for a camping trip | *She is wrong: it means a rich mix of many different things | She is right, it is a cloth on a wall | It means a sad story about a family
exam: «Louise Bourgeois said her spider stood for her mother, who repaired tapestries.» What does repaired tapestries show? | *Her mother mended the heavy picture cloths | Her mother was a builder | Her mother painted the walls of the house | Her mother sold fish at the market
